    <description>SHARED ERROR-HANDLING FRAMEWORK (Centellic diagnostic Stabilise #1). Drop this subflow into ANY flow's fault path to log the failure to Flow_Log__c instead of letting it surface raw. Fail-open: its own DML/alert faults are swallowed so it can never break the caller. Logging is unconditional; email alerting is opt-in via Fault_Alert_Setting__mdt.Default (Alert_Enabled, default false). USAGE: on a DML/lookup/action element add a Fault connector to a subflow call of Platform_Fault_Logger, passing in_FlowApiName, in_Context (element or stage), in_RecordId, in_RecordName, and in_ErrorMessage = {!$Flow.FaultMessage}.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>frm_AlertBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;Flow: &apos; &amp; {!in_FlowApiName} &amp; &apos;  |  Context: &apos; &amp; {!in_Context} &amp; &apos;  |  Record: &apos; &amp; {!in_RecordName} &amp; &apos; (&apos; &amp; {!in_RecordId} &amp; &apos;)  |  Severity: &apos; &amp; {!in_Severity} &amp; &apos;  |  Error: &apos; &amp; {!in_ErrorMessage}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frm_AlertSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;[SF Fault] &apos; &amp; {!in_FlowApiName} &amp; &apos; on &apos; &amp; {!in_RecordName}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>frm_ClassName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;[&apos; &amp; {!in_Severity} &amp; &apos;] &apos; &amp; LEFT({!in_Context}, 240)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Platform Fault Logger {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Platform Fault Logger</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
